{"choices":[{"message":{"content":"```json\n{\n  \"quantitative_comparisons\": [\n    {\n      \"research_object\": \"TACITO trial (P0593)\",\n      \"result_or_measure\": \"12-month PFS rate\",\n      \"setting_or_time\": \"metastatic RCC, first-line pembrolizumab + axitinib\",\n      \"groups\": [\n        {\"group\": \"d-FMT\", \"value\": \"70%\"},\n        {\"group\": \"p-FMT\", \"value\": \"41%\"}\n      ],\n      \"reported_statistics\": \"P = 0.053\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"research_object\": \"TACITO trial (P0593)\",\n      \"result_or_measure\": \"median PFS\",\n      \"setting_or_time\": \"metastatic RCC, first-line pembrolizumab + axitinib\",\n      \"groups\": [\n        {\"group\": \"d-FMT\", \"value\": \"24.0 months\"},\n        {\"group\": \"p-FMT\", \"value\": \"9.0 months\"}\n      ],\n      \"reported_statistics\": \"HR = 0.50, P = 0.035\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"research_object\": \"TACITO trial (P0593)\",\n      \"result_or_measure\": \"median OS\",\n      \"setting_or_time\": \"metastatic RCC, first-line pembrolizumab + axitinib\",\n      \"groups\": [\n        {\"group\": \"d-FMT\", \"value\": \"41.0 months\"},\n        {\"group\": \"p-FMT\", \"value\": \"28.3 months\"}\n      ],\n      \"reported_statistics\": \"P = 0.167\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"research_object\": \"TACITO trial (P0593)\",\n      \"result_or_measure\": \"ORR\",\n      \"setting_or_time\": \"metastatic RCC, first-line pembrolizumab + axitinib\",\n      \"groups\": [\n        {\"group\": \"d-FMT\", \"value\": \"52%\"},\n        {\"group\": \"p-FMT\", \"value\": \"32%\"}\n      ],\n      \"reported_statistics\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"research_object\": \"MITRIC trial (P0578)\",\n      \"result_or_measure\": \"ORR\",\n      \"setting_or_time\": \"ICI-refractory advanced cancers (melanoma, HNSCC, RCC, MSI-H pancreatic)\",\n      \"groups\": [\n        {\"group\": \"FMT + ICI\", \"value\": \"0%\"}\n      ],\n      \"reported_statistics\": \"n=12\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"research_object\": \"MITRIC trial (P0578)\",\n      \"result_or_measure\": \"median PFS\",\n      \"setting_or_time\": \"ICI-refractory advanced cancers\",\n      \"groups\": [\n        {\"group\": \"FMT + ICI\", \"value\": \"1.5 months\"}\n      ],\n      \"reported_statistics\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"research_object\": \"MITRIC trial (P0578)\",\n      \"result_or_measure\": \"median OS\",\n      \"setting_or_time\": \"ICI-refractory advanced cancers\",\n      \"groups\": [\n        {\"group\": \"FMT + ICI\", \"value\": \"10.1 months\"}\n      ],\n      \"reported_statistics\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"research_object\": \"MIMic trial (P0577)\",\n      \"result_or_measure\": \"ORR\",\n      \"setting_or_time\": \"treatment-naïve advanced melanoma, first-line anti-PD1 + FMT\",\n      \"groups\": [\n        {\"group\": \"FMT + anti-PD1\", \"value\": \"65%\"}\n      ],\n      \"reported_statistics\": \"n=20\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"research_object\": \"MIMic trial (P0577)\",\n      \"result_or_measure\": \"median PFS\",\n      \"setting_or_time\": \"treatment-naïve advanced melanoma\",\n      \"groups\": [\n        {\"group\": \"FMT + anti-PD1\", \"value\": \"29.6 months\"}\n      ],\n      \"reported_statistics\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"research_object\": \"MIMic trial (P0577)\",\n      \"result_or_measure\": \"median OS\",\n      \"setting_or_time\": \"treatment-naïve advanced melanoma\",\n      \"groups\": [\n        {\"group\": \"FMT + anti-PD1\", \"value\": \"52.8 months\"}\n      ],\n      \"reported_statistics\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"research_object\": \"FMT-LUMINate NSCLC cohort (P0583)\",\n      \"result_or_measure\": \"ORR\",\n      \"setting_or_time\": \"NSCLC, anti-PD-1 monotherapy + FMT\",\n      \"groups\": [\n        {\"group\": \"FMT + anti-PD-1\", \"value\": \"80%\"}\n      ],\n      \"reported_statistics\": \"n=20\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"research_object\": \"FMT-LUMINate Melanoma cohort (P0583)\",\n      \"result_or_measure\": \"ORR\",\n      \"setting_or_time\": \"melanoma, dual anti-PD-1 + anti-CTLA-4 + FMT\",\n      \"groups\": [\n        {\"group\": \"FMT + dual ICI\", \"value\": \"75%\"}\n      ],\n      \"reported_statistics\": \"n=20\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"research_object\": \"FMT-LUMINate dual ICI melanoma (P0591)\",\n      \"result_or_measure\": \"ORR\",\n      \"setting_or_time\": \"previously untreated advanced melanoma, dual ICI + FMT\",\n      \"groups\": [\n        {\"group\": \"FMT + dual ICI\", \"value\": \"70%\"}\n      ],\n      \"reported_statistics\": \"n=20\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"research_object\": \"FMT-LUMINate dual ICI melanoma (P0591)\",\n      \"result_or_measure\": \"Grade >3 irAE rate\",\n      \"setting_or_time\": \"previously untreated advanced melanoma\",\n      \"groups\": [\n        {\"group\": \"FMT + dual ICI\", \"value\": \"65%\"}\n      ],\n      \"reported_statistics\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"research_object\": \"Kim et al. study (P0594)\",\n      \"result_or_measure\": \"ORR\",\n      \"setting_or_time\": \"ICI-refractory advanced solid cancers (gastric, esophageal, hepatocellular)\",\n      \"groups\": [\n        {\"group\": \"FMT + anti-PD-1\", \"value\": \"7.7%\"}\n      ],\n      \"reported_statistics\": \"n=13\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"research_object\": \"Kim et al. study (P0594)\",\n      \"result_or_measure\": \"DCR\",\n      \"setting_or_time\": \"ICI-refractory advanced solid cancers\",\n      \"groups\": [\n        {\"group\": \"FMT + anti-PD-1\", \"value\": \"46.2%\"}\n      ],\n      \"reported_statistics\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"research_object\": \"RENMIN-215 trial (P0636)\",\n      \"result_or_measure\": \"ORR\",\n      \"setting_or_time\": \"MSS colorectal cancer, FMT + ICIs\",\n      \"groups\": [\n        {\"group\": \"FMT + ICIs\", \"value\": \"20%\"}\n      ],\n      \"reported_statistics\": \"Phase II\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"research_object\": \"RENMIN-215 trial (P0636)\",\n      \"result_or_measure\": \"median PFS\",\n      \"setting_or_time\": \"MSS colorectal cancer\",\n      \"groups\": [\n        {\"group\": \"FMT + ICIs\", \"value\": \"9.6 months\"}\n      ],\n      \"reported_statistics\": \"\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"usable_content\": \"当前材料中未发现已完成并发表主要结局数据的大型随机对照 III 期临床试验（Phase III RCT）证实微生物干预（如 FMT）在 ICI 治疗实体瘤中的疗效。现有最高证据等级为 IIa 期随机对照试验和多项单臂 I/II 期试验。TACITO 试验（P0593）是唯一报道的随机、双盲、安慰剂对照 IIa 期试验（n=45），在转移性肾细胞癌一线治疗中，供体 FMT 组中位 PFS 显著优于安慰剂组（24.0 vs 9.0 个月，HR=0.50，P=0.035），但主要终点（12 个月 PFS 率）未达统计学显著性（70% vs 41%，P=0.053），总生存期差异亦不显著（41.0 vs 28.3 个月，P=0.167）。其他研究均为单臂试验：MITRIC 试验（P0578，n=12）在 ICI 耐药人群中 ORR 为 0%，中位 PFS 仅 1.5 个月；MIMic 试验（P0577，n=20）在初治黑色素瘤中 ORR 65%、中位 PFS 29.6 个月；FMT-LUMINate 试验（P0583/P0591）在 NSCLC 和黑色素瘤队列中 ORR 分别为 80% 和 70-75%，但伴随较高的 3 级以上免疫相关不良事件（65%）。多项材料（P0584、P0636）明确指出当前临床管线以早期试验为主，截至 2025 年 6 月的调查未发现已完成并发表主要终点的 III 期 RCT，且呼吁未来研究应优先开展大型随机对照试验。FMT 疗效呈现高度情境依赖性：一线治疗场景（如 TACITO、MIMic、FMT-LUMINate）信号优于 ICI 耐药挽救治疗场景（如 MITRIC、Kim et al.），且供体选择（ICI 响应者 vs 健康供体）、给药方案、患者基线状态（疾病进展速度、免疫微环境）均影响结局。\",\n  \"decision\": \"external_research\",\n  \"answers_requested_question\": false,\n  \"still_missing\": \"已完成并发表主要结局数据的 Phase III RCT 证据\",\n  \"read_focus\": \"无需再读当前材料，已确认这些材料中无 Phase III RCT 数据\",\n  \"external_ask\": \"需在 ClinicalTrials.gov、WHO ICTRP 或近期会议摘要/新闻稿中系统检索 2024-2026 年间完成的微生物干预 +ICI 的 Phase III 随机对照试验（如 CanBiome2 NCT06623461、ME.17 NCT06623461 等）的完成状态和主要结局发表情况，以确认是否存在材料未覆盖的已发表 III 期数据\",\n  \"reason\": \"问题要求确认\"已完成的大型随机对照 III 期临床试验\"，但所有提供材料最高仅至 IIa 期（TACITO）或单臂 I/II 期。虽然多项材料（尤其是 P0636 截至 2025 年 6 月的调查）明确指出无已完成 III 期 RCT，但确认\"不存在\"这类阴性结论需要外部注册库系统检索验证，不能仅依赖现有材料未提及来断定。成功标准（找到已发表主要结局数据的 Phase III RCT）未满足。\"\n}\n```","reasoning_content":"The user is asking whether there are completed large-scale Phase III randomized controlled trials (RCTs) confirming the efficacy of microbiome interventions (like FMT) in ICI-treated solid tumors.\n\nI need to check the provided materials for any mention of completed Phase III RCTs with published primary outcome data (OS/PFS).\n\nLooking at the materials:\n1. P0578 (MITRIC trial): Explicitly stated as a \"single-arm phase IIa basket trial\". Not Phase III, not randomized. ORR 0%, median PFS 1.5 months.\n2. P0593 (TACITO trial): Explicitly stated as a \"phase 2a\" randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial. Primary endpoint (12-month PFS rate) not met (P=0.053), but secondary endpoint (median PFS) showed improvement (24.0 vs 9.0 months, P=0.035). Not Phase III.\n3. P0594 (Kim et al., 2024): Explicitly stated as a \"prospective, single-arm, single-center study\" (Phase II). Not Phase III.\n4. P0577 (MIMic trial): Explicitly stated as a \"phase I multicenter trial\". Mentions a planned Phase II randomized trial (ME.17). Not Phase III.\n5. P0583 (FMT-LUMINate): Explicitly stated as a \"phase 2 trial\". Mentions CanBiome2 (NCT06623461) as an upcoming randomized trial (128 patients), but results not reported here. Not Phase III.\n6. P0584 (Narrative review): States \"large-scale, multicenter, standardized longitudinal studies are needed\" and \"substantial hurdles remain\". No Phase III trials reported.\n7. P0591 (FMT-LUMINate abstract): Phase II trial.\n8. P0602 (TACITO summary): Confirms Phase 2a.\n9. P0616 (MITRIC abstract): Confirms Phase IIa.\n10. P0636 (Survey of trials): States \"pipeline is predominantly early-phase (Phase I, I/II, and II), with no mention of completed Phase 3 randomized controlled trials (RCTs) publishing primary endpoints\".\n11. P0592 (Bibliometric study): Calls for \"Future research should prioritize large-scale randomized controlled trials\".\n\nNone of the materials report a completed Phase III RCT with published primary outcome data. The highest level of evidence found is Phase IIa (TACITO, MITRIC, FMT-LUMINate, etc.). Several materials explicitly state that Phase III data is lacking or that future research should prioritize Phase III trials.\n\nThe question asks specifically about \"completed large-scale Phase III RCTs\". Based on the materials, the answer is negative - no such trials are reported in the provided literature. The materials consistently indicate that current evidence is limited to Phase I/II trials.\n\nI need to:\n1. Create quantitative_comparisons if there are any numerical data from trials (even if not Phase III, to show the current state of evidence)\n2. Write usable_content explaining that no Phase III RCTs are found, but Phase IIa data exists\n3. Set decision appropriately (external_research might be needed to confirm no Phase III exists beyond these materials, but the materials themselves suggest none exist)\n4. Set answers_requested_question to false since the success criteria (finding a Phase III RCT) is not met\n\nLet me extract quantitative data from the trials mentioned:\n\nP0593 (TACITO):\n- d-FMT arm: 12-month PFS rate 70%, median PFS 24.0 months, median OS 41.0 months, ORR 52%\n- p-FMT arm: 12-month PFS rate 41%, median PFS 9.0 months, median OS 28.3 months, ORR 32%\n- P-value for primary endpoint: 0.053\n- P-value for median PFS: 0.035\n- P-value for OS: 0.167\n- n=45 randomized (45 in full analysis set)\n\nP0578 (MITRIC):\n- ORR: 0%\n- median PFS: 1.5 months\n- median OS: 10.1 months\n- n=12 patients\n\nP0577 (MIMic):\n- ORR: 65%\n- median PFS: 29.6 months\n- median OS: 52.8 months\n- n=20 patients\n\nP0583 (FMT-LUMINate NSCLC):\n- ORR: 80%\n- n=20 NSCLC patients\n\nP0583 (FMT-LUMINate Melanoma):\n- ORR: 75%\n- n=20 melanoma patients\n\nP0591 (FMT-LUMINate dual ICI melanoma):\n- ORR: 70%\n- Grade >3 irAE: 65%\n- n=20 patients\n\nP0594 (Kim et al.):\n- ORR: 7.7%\n- DCR: 46.2%\n- n=13 recipients\n\nP0636 (RENMIN-215):\n- ORR: 20%\n- median PFS: 9.6 months\n- Phase II trial in MSS CRC\n\nI should organize these as quantitative_comparisons where there are direct comparisons (like TACITO which is randomized). For single-arm trials, I can still report the results but note they are not comparative.\n\nFor decision: The materials clearly indicate no Phase III RCTs are found. However, to definitively answer \"whether there ARE any completed Phase III RCTs\" (a negative claim), I might need external verification beyond these materials. But the materials themselves (especially P0636 survey and multiple trial reports) consistently state Phase III data is lacking. I'll set decision to external_research because confirming a negative (no Phase III exists) ideally requires a systematic registry search, but the usable_content can clearly state what the current materials show.\n\nActually, looking at the instructions: \"对于\"是否已经有某类研究/结果\"的问题，找到一个符合条件的实例可以回答；几篇论文未提到，或一篇较早综述说当时没有，不能回答当前是否存在。\" - This means for \"whether there already exists\" questions, finding one instance can answer yes, but multiple papers not mentioning it or an earlier review saying none existed cannot definitively answer no for the current time.\n\nHowever, P0636 is a survey as of June 30, 2025, which explicitly states \"no mention of completed Phase 3 randomized controlled trials (RCTs) publishing primary endpoints\". This is relatively current. But to be rigorous, I should note that external verification via registry search would strengthen the negative claim.\n\nI'll set:\n- decision: external_research (because confirming absence of Phase III trials ideally needs registry verification)\n- answers_requested_question: false (success criteria not met - no Phase III RCT found in materials)\n- usable_content: Clearly state current evidence level (Phase IIa max), summarize key trial results, note the absence of Phase III data\n\nLet me structure the quantitative_comparisons properly for the randomized trial (TACITO) and note single-arm trials separately.","role":"assistant"},"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"logprobs":null}],"object":"chat.completion","usage":{"prompt_tokens":19753,"completion_tokens":4369,"total_tokens":24122,"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1648,"text_tokens":4369},"prompt_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":19753}},"created":1791128461,"system_fingerprint":null,"mo